<Base title="Research">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Research</h1>
    <div class="grid"><p class="span-8">I do applied HCI: how designed systems land in real institutions, and what that means for method. Schools, care homes, vans, card tables.</p></div>
  </header>

  <Section label="Doctorate" title="Thesis">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p><em>Towards Design of Interaction Systems for Constrained Spaces.</em> University of Waterloo, 2025, supervised by Mark Hancock. I study what happens when technology designed for large, stable environments is used in small, moving, improvised ones: vans, cockpits, classrooms, card tables. The work runs from field studies to physical artefacts.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Current" title="In progress">
    <ul>
      <li>Proteus Card Deck: affordable, scalable, and familiar electronic cards. With Oliver Schneider and Mark Hancock. CHI PLAY 2026.</li>
      <li>Designing supportive haptic technologies for NICU mothers. With M. Prakash, S. G. Sehl, Y. Li, T. S. Pawar, and C. MacArthur. In revision for DIS 2027.</li>
      <li>A/B Testing IRL. Textbook chapter, Springer, 2026.</li>
      <li>How field-site access strategies compound and transfer across studies. Methods paper for Graphics Interface 2026.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Published" title="Refereed papers">
    <ul>
      <li>Rizvi, A. H. (2026). Embed, don't isolate: designing holistic dashboards for stigma-sensitive parent communication. <em>ACM Interactive Health (IH '26)</em>. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3786579.3804955">doi</a></li>
      <li>Rizvi, A. H., &amp; Hancock, M. (2024). Small spaces, many places: a phenomenological analysis of technology-mediated placemaking in small spaces. <em>Graphics Interface (GI '24)</em>. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3670947.3670966">doi</a></li>
      <li>Rizvi, A. H., Morayko, K., Hancock, M., &amp; Song, A. (2021). Provocations from #vanlife: investigating life and work in a community extensively using technology not designed for them. <em>CHI 2021</em>.</li>
      <li>Rizvi, A. H., Singh, L. P., &amp; Bhardwaj, A. (2009). Human integration matrix: an adaptive framework to enhance human systems integration in new product development. <em>PICMET '09</em>.</li>
      <li>Rizvi, A. H., &amp; Sachdeva, A. (2009). Optimization of retail clusters by improving individual store performance. <em>PICMET '09</em>.</li>
